request: Rename the `watched` field of watchlist items to `seen` everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> movie, watchlist-store, watchlist  (Rename the watchlist item status field `watched` to `seen` everywhere it appears: the item interfaces in movie, the store's item creation/toggling/counting and its persisted key, and the watchlist component's derived signals and template bindings. Public API names (watchedCount, toggleWatched) are not item fields and stay unchanged. Existing tests referencing the old field name will surface as change requests to approve next round.)
round 1: owners movie=ok watchlist-store=ok watchlist=rejected; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist  (Round 1 applied the rename in movie and watchlist-store. Every remaining oracle error is in the watchlist unit: the component template still binds item.watched (3 Angular compiler errors) and the spec asserts store.items()[0].watched. The owner's requested test edit merely updates that assertion to the renamed field, which the request calls for, so I approve it and re-instruct watchlist.)
round 2: owners watchlist=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 3: plan -> watchlist-store, watchlist  (The watched→seen field rename is complete and correct: tsc is clean and all 33 unit tests pass. All 5 remaining failures are in my own acceptance tests, caused by test-harness mistakes rather than product defects: (1) my watchlist-store test called `new WatchlistStore()` outside any injection context although the store's constructor-time effect() requires one (NG0203), and (2) my watchlist component test rendered the template's RouterLink without router providers (NG0201 ActivatedRoute). This round only replaces those two acceptance tests — store obtained via TestBed (persistence given time to settle before asserting the serialized keys), provideRouter([]) added to the component test. No production code changes are needed; owners of both units are explicitly told to submit with zero file changes.)
round 3: owners watchlist-store=ok watchlist=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 4: accept  (The watched→seen field rename is applied everywhere: Movie and WatchItem interfaces expose seen, the store and watchlist component read/write seen, and persisted JSON uses the seen key. tsc is clean and all 38 tests pass, including the acceptance tests pinning the new behaviour.)

